X is a Y  => X ~ Y
X is an Y => X is a Y

has property   is a ->
has part       is a ->
is opposite of is a ->

"is attribute of" is opposite of "has attribute"
"is part of"      is opposite of "has part"
"is for example"  is opposite of "is a"

"has part"      has attribute transitive
"has attribute" has attribute transitive
~               has attribute transitive

R has attribute transitive, X R Y, Y R Z => X R Z
X has attribute E, E is a K  => X has attribute K
X has part P,      P is a K  => X has part K
K has attribute E, X is a K  => X has attribute E
K has part P,      X is a K  => X has part P
X is opposite of Y, X is a K => Y is a K
X is opposite of Y           => Y is opposite of X
R is opposite of S, X R Y    => Y S X

X is opposite of Y, A has attribute X, A has attribute Y => !
X is opposite of Y, A has part X, A has part Y => !
X is opposite of Y, A is a X, A is a Y => !
X has attribute E, X is a E     => !
X has attribute E, E is a X     => !
X has attribute E, E has part X => !

X is a thing             => X has attribute color
X is a thing             => X has attribute weight
X has part Y, X != thing => X is a thing
X has part Y, Y != thing => X is a thing

generates is a ->
needs is a ->

"is needed by" is opposite of needs
"is generated by" is opposite of generates

is needed by is opposite of needs
is generated by  is opposite of generates

X generates energy  => X is an "energy source"
A has attribute hot => A generates heat
A generates oxygen  => A has attribute alive


chimpanzee is an ape
ape has attribute alive

chimpanzee has part hand
hand has part finger

"green mint" is an mint

"water mint" is a mint

peppermint is an mint

mint is a lamiacea

catnip is a lamiacea

"green mint" has attribute sweet
